PR #109 Terra/high final review — exact `cf722a999cb449acf4b992d2d4fd7787a363144c`

**BLOCKED** on one Important data-preservation defect, independently reproduced on SQLite and PostgreSQL 16 despite five green hosted checks:

- Migration 12 inserts legacy `run.stdout`/`run.stderr` into `run_legacy_output_archive` using `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, then drops the source columns. If an archive row already exists for the same `run_id` with different/partial values, the whole incoming row is skipped and distinct non-null source data is silently lost.

Smallest required repair:
- fieldwise preserve compatible/null values;
- if archive and source contain unequal non-null values for the same field, abort transactionally before dropping either source column;
- prove no-column/fresh/null, partial merge, equal collision, unequal collision rollback, rerun and retry-after-operator-resolution on SQLite and PostgreSQL;
- preserve every previously accepted database, redaction, lock, migration, archive and recovery boundary.

No other blocker. One sole writer is assigned; a new exact SHA will receive fresh hosted checks and Terra review.

PR #115 independent exact-SHA browser acceptance — `16da9717822cabc33ca39d39ca896aae7280b0fb`

